From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 dockable hosted DevTools (ABI 1.54)

Bridge 0.57.0, feature devtools_docking. With a dock callback set, hosted
frontends open with can_dock=true as DevToolsWindow::GetDevToolsURL does, so
the frontend shows Dock side, the device toolbar and toggle-dock. setIsDocked
and setInspectedPageBounds reach the host with the side Chromium's
DevToolsSettings reads from the profile's currentDockState preference, which
the frontend persists itself. As DevToolsWindow, the undocked frontend's
device-mode toolbox (device_mode_emulation_frame.html) is marked at
WebContentsCreated, kept rendering, adopted as a locked registry tab,
replaced when a reloaded frontend opens a new one, and closed with its
frontend. No upstream file changes; without a callback the
frontend URL and behaviour are tab/058's.

Last rebased: 2026-11-09 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

